<%# ** THE THREE TILES (two-shapes spec §4). ** Local: `presenter` (BudgetPagePresenter).

      ┌ Your rules need ────────┐ ┌ You bring in ──────┐ ┌ Left over ─────┐
      │ $1,668.00 a period      │ │ $2,400.00 a period │ │ $732.00        │
      │ ▮▮▮▮▮▮▮▮▮▮▯▯▯▯          │ │ biweekly · change  │ │ your rules fit │
      │ Bills $1,400 · Usage …  │ └────────────────────┘ └────────────────┘
      └─────────────────────────┘

    ** THEY ARE THE STRUCTURAL CHECK AND THE TYPE OVERVIEW, WHICH BOTH DIED HERE (§7). ** The check
    was three labelled figures in a definition list under a heading asking "Does this fit your
    income?" and the overview was a sentence above the groups; they are the same three numbers and
    the same split, said at the top of the page where the question is asked. Nothing was dropped:
    the sacrifice door is on the third tile, and the declaration form is one click behind "change".

    EVERY FIGURE IS `standing_ask` — a constant of the rules and the grid — and never Σ claims,
    which is this afternoon's answer and would report a different split tomorrow with nothing
    edited. That is also what makes the bands add up to the figure above them. %>
<%# ** AT 375 THE NEED TILE SPANS AND THE OTHER TWO HALVE THE ROW BENEATH IT (mobile pass,
    2026-09-06). ** Stacked one under the other the three tiles were 362px tall, which put the FIRST
    ROW OF THE LIST at y=659 — below a 667px screen, so a phone opening the Budget page saw three
    tiles and no budget. Measured. Halving the second row brings the list back above the fold and
    costs nothing: the two half tiles hold `$12,500.00` and `$11,674.07` at `text-xl` inside 133px of
    content box.

    ** THE ORDER IS THE DOM'S AND THAT IS THE POINT. ** Need spans because it is the widest thing on
    the page — a bar and three labelled bands — and because leaving it beside income would break the
    reading: income and left over are the two halves of ONE subtraction and belong on one line.

    ** AND THE UNIT DROPS TO ITS OWN LINE BELOW `md`. ** Inline, `$12,500.00 a period` broke at the
    space the box ran out at — measured as `$12,500.00 a` over `period`, a phrase cut in half under
    a figure. `block` puts the break where the meaning is: the money, then what it is per. %>
<section class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3" data-tiles>
  <%# TILE 1 — WHAT THE RULES ASK OF A PERIOD, and what kind of rules they are. %>
  <div class="col-span-2 bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded p-4 sm:col-span-1 sm:px-5 sm:py-4" data-tile="need">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Your rules need</h2>
    <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 tabular-nums" data-tile-figure>
      <%= number_to_currency(presenter.tiles.need) %> <span class="block text-sm font-normal text-gray-500 md:inline">a period</span>
    </p>

    <% if presenter.tiles.segments.any? %>
      <%# ONE BAR, ONE BAND PER KIND, in the same three colours the rows' dots and Home's stripes
          use — `HomeHelper::STRIPE_FILLS`, one table, so a bill is the same colour on every screen.
          The percentages are the presenter's (`Segment#percent`), so the bar and the figures under
          it are two readings of one number rather than two derivations of it. %>
      <div class="mt-3 flex h-2 overflow-hidden rounded bg-gray-100" data-type-bar>
        <% presenter.tiles.segments.each do |segment| %>
          <div class="<%= type_fill(segment.type) %>"
               style="width: <%= segment.percent %>%;"
               data-type-band="<%= segment.type %>"></div>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <%# THE SEPARATOR IS ITS OWN ELEMENT AND `aria-hidden`, so a screen reader reads three figures
          rather than three interpuncts. A TYPE WITH NO RULES IS ABSENT rather than printed as
          $0.00 — a figure that is true and reports nothing, on a line whose whole job is the split. %>
      <p class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-xs text-gray-700">
        <% presenter.tiles.segments.each_with_index do |segment, index| %>
          <% unless index.zero? %>
            <span class="text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <% end %>
          <span data-type-total="<%= segment.type %>">
            <span class="text-gray-500"><%= rule_type_heading(segment.type) %></span>
            <span class="font-medium text-gray-900 tabular-nums"><%= number_to_currency(segment.amount) %></span>
          </span>
        <% end %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# TILE 2 — WHAT THE USER SAYS THEY BRING IN, and the one door to changing it. %>
  <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded p-4 sm:px-5 sm:py-4" data-tile="income">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">You bring in</h2>
    <% if presenter.tiles.declared? %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 tabular-nums" data-tile-figure>
        <%= number_to_currency(presenter.tiles.income) %> <span class="block text-sm font-normal text-gray-500 md:inline">a period</span>
      </p>
      <%# ** THE ONE DOOR ONTO THE DECLARATION, AND ON A PHONE IT HAS TO BE PRESSABLE. ** It measured
          42×14 — a fourteen-pixel target for the only control that can change the period every
          figure on this page is divided by. `min-h-10` is 40px of box around the same word; the
          line's own height is unchanged above `sm`, where a pointer does not need it.

          ** THE LINE IS TEXT FLOW AND NOT A FLEX ROW (fix round — L2). ** It was briefly
          `flex gap-1`, which replaced the interpunct's own word spacing with a 4px gap at EVERY
          width — a desktop change made in passing for a mobile target. `inline-flex` on the link
          alone buys the box without touching the sentence around it. %>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-500">
        <span data-tile-cadence><%= presenter.tiles.cadence.humanize %></span> ·
        <%= link_to "change",
                    budget_page_path(declare: 1),
                    class: "inline-flex min-h-10 items-center text-brand-dark hover:text-brand underline sm:min-h-0",
                    data: { declare_link: true } %>
      </p>
    <% else %>
      <%# NOT YET SAID IS NOT ZERO. Zero is a claim about the user's income; this is the absence of
          one, and the tile invites rather than reporting. %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-500" data-tile-figure>Not said yet</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs">
        <%= link_to "Declare your income",
                    budget_page_path(declare: 1),
                    class: "inline-flex min-h-10 items-center text-brand-dark hover:text-brand underline sm:min-h-0",
                    data: { declare_link: true } %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# TILE 3 — THE SUBTRACTION, GREEN WHEN IT FITS AND RED WHEN IT DOES NOT (§4). %>
  <div class="bg-white border rounded p-4 sm:px-5 sm:py-4 <%= presenter.tiles.declared? && !presenter.tiles.fits? ? "border-status-danger" : "border-gray-200" %>"
       data-tile="leftover">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Left over</h2>
    <% if presenter.tiles.declared? %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-semibold tabular-nums <%= presenter.tiles.fits? ? "text-status-success" : "text-status-danger" %>"
         data-tile-figure>
        <%= number_to_currency(presenter.tiles.leftover) %>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-500" data-tile-verdict>
        <%= presenter.tiles.fits? ? "Your rules fit what you bring in." : "Your rules ask for more than you bring in." %>
      </p>

      <%# §9: THE ONE SCREEN THAT MUST NOT OFFER MOVING MONEY AS THE ANSWER. Reallocation cannot fix
          a budget that does not fit an income, and `sacrifice_path` refuses in exactly the two
          states this button is not shown in — nothing declared, or the budget already fitting — so
          the route's gate and this one are the same condition read twice. %>
      <% unless presenter.tiles.fits? %>
        <%= link_to("What could you cut?",
                    sacrifice_path,
                    class: "mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2.5 rounded border sm:py-1.5 " \
                           "border-status-danger bg-status-danger-light text-status-danger " \
                           "text-xs font-medium hover:bg-white",
                    data: { sacrifice_link: true }) %>
      <% end %>
    <% else %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-500" data-tile-figure>
        <%= link_to "Declare your income", budget_page_path(declare: 1), class: "text-brand-dark hover:text-brand underline" %>
        and this will say whether your rules fit.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>
